From 3d98178c227b8904921c71ddfc73d8a9d80802b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:34:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: tune - search Forge AI profile settings against real win
 rates

Why: simulated meta win rates barely track real ones (rank correlation
0.24) because Forge's AI pilots creature decks better than control and
value decks. Forge steers its AI with profile files (AiProps keys), so
this adds custom profiles without touching the Forge tree, and a search
over profile settings that guards against fitting eleven noisy numbers.

What it does
- Every run gets its own profile folder RUN_DIR/ai (Forge's res/ai copied
  unchanged + mtgsim/profiles/*.ai|*.json + MTGSIM_HOME/profiles + run-
  generated profiles); the driver loads it via -Dmtgsim.aiProfileDir after
  FModel.initialize and names it in the ready line; the runner refuses a
  driver that does not. The driver also refuses a profile name it did not
  load (Forge would silently use the AiProps enum defaults, which are not
  Default.ai). run.json records each used profile's settings hash and the
  Forge build fingerprint. cli._check_profile_name accepts shipped/user
  profiles. New module mtgsim/ai_profiles.py.
- python3 -m mtgsim tune (mtgsim/tune.py): one profile per archetype group
  (default reactive=control,midrange,tempo; proactive=aggro,ramp,combo),
  --profiles K random profiles per tuned group drawn from a parameter space
  (mtgsim/profiles/spaces/default.json, 21 params with a reason each,
  change probability 0.2), candidates = every combination incl. baseline.
  Objective: Spearman of deck sim vs real win rate over training decks
  (Pearson, mean gap too; optional --matchups file, --objective). Guards:
  --holdout decks never used for selection, --cv loo on round-1 games,
  paired binomial-resampling noise ranges, --confirm on fresh game indices,
  data-needed statement (Fisher z). Cache: RUN_DIR/cache.jsonl keyed by
  engine fingerprint, seed, format, mc, timeout, per deck fingerprint+name+
  effective profile hash, plus game index; successive halving (--rounds
  10,30 --eta 3); --resume; --import of earlier runs; --dry-run plan.

Done and verified
- Full suite under the engine lock: 235 tests OK in 123 s (229 unit incl.
  39 in tests/test_tune.py; integration incl. new
  tests/test_integration_profiles.py: 60 Forests mulligan under Default,
  never with MULLIGAN_THRESHOLD=8; unknown profile -> engine error).
- Metric code reproduces the 1,650-game baseline (runs/baseline-rr-n30-s1,
  seed 1, 30 games/pairing, all 1,650 games import as identical):
  Spearman 0.236, game-noise 0.12-0.35, Pearson 0.23, mean gap 13.0 pts;
  first 10 games/pairing only: 0.29, noise 0.06-0.41.
- Smoke run (4 decks: Boros Dwarves, Mono-Green Landfall, Dimir Midrange,
  Orzhov Lifegain; space = MULLIGAN_THRESHOLD=8 only; --profiles 1 for both
  groups = 4 candidates; --rounds 4,8 --eta 2 --confirm 4; 168 games, ~5
  min incl. JVM starts):
  * probe-profile seats mulliganed 0 of 232 seat-games; Default 76 of 256
  * same seed, a deck's profile changed: 44 of 112 games differ, 68
    identical (games where Default kept its hand anyway)
  * 60/60 comparable baseline games identical to runs/baseline-rr-n30-s1
    (old driver, Forge's own profile folder)
  * round 1 played 80 games for 96 results used, round 2 44 for 96;
    --resume of the finished run played 0 games, same result.
- Dry-run plans for the 11 meta decks, holdout Dimir Uldaros + Boros
  Dragons, --import runs/baseline-rr-n30-s1 (85 games/min):
  * defaults (--profiles 3 = 16 candidates, --rounds 10,30, --confirm 30):
    ~12,570 games, ~149 min
  * --tune reactive --profiles 6 --rounds 10,20 --confirm 20 (7
    candidates): ~6,270 games, ~75 min
  * --profiles 2 (9 candidates): ~8,520 games, ~102 min

Not done
- No real tuning run (left for the user to schedule; engine time is
  sequenced). Nothing has been tuned, so mtgsim/profiles/ ships no profile
  yet, only the search space.
- Data needed: over 11 decks, Spearman 0.24 has a 95% interval of -0.44 to
  0.74; +/-0.2 needs ~90 decks at r=0.24 (60 at 0.5, 30 at 0.7), +/-0.1
  ~360/230/110; matchup data needs ~97 real matches per matchup for +/-10
  points.

Next steps
1. Final review of the diff; turn this into a normal commit (drop "WIP:").
2. Hand over the real-experiment command (pilot first if time is short):
   flock <lock> setsid nohup python3 -m mtgsim tune --holdout "Dimir
   Uldaros" "Boros Dragons" --import runs/baseline-rr-n30-s1 --out
   runs/tune-meta-s1 > runs/tune-meta-s1.log 2>&1 &   (~2.5 h)
   Pilot: add --tune reactive --profiles 6 --rounds 10,20 --confirm 20
   (~75 min). Check with --dry-run first; --resume runs/tune-meta-s1 after
   an interruption.
3. After the run: if a candidate clears noise on training and held-out
   decks, copy best/tuned-<group>.json into mtgsim/profiles/ and record
   the result in VALIDATION.md and decks/standard/meta/README.md.

Side finding: Forge's PlayerControllerAi.setupAutoProfile pilots a deck as
non-aggro when its name contains "Control" or its average mana value is
above 3, so deck names change play; the cache key includes deck names.

